### `CONNECT relay stagnation`

| Symptom | Cause | Fix |
| ------- | ----- | --- |
| Apps (TikTok search, Chrome, …) get slower/stuttery the longer PROXY stays up; restarting the proxy makes them snappy again. Some features “fail” then work after leaving the app. | CONNECT tunnels (HTTP/2 keep-alives) never idle-out. Each holds **2** `zt-relay` threads + **1** `Dispatchers.IO` thread. Old **fixed 64** pool deadlocks at **32** concurrent CONNECTs (both pumps queued, neither runs). System DNS also 6s-NXDOMAIN then negative-cache bursts (`Unable to resolve host …: No address associated with hostname`) — leave-app / retry recovers. | Cached relay pool (`newCachedThreadPool`) + **60s shared idle** timeout (`ProxyRelay`). Java sockets poll every 5s and check last-byte either direction. ZeroTierInputStream maps `SO_RCVTIMEO` to EOF — do **not** use the 5s poll on ZT; set ZT recv timeout to the idle window. Watch: if 60s is too aggressive (video pause / HTTP/2 PING slower than 60s), raise `DEFAULT_IDLE_TIMEOUT_MS`. DNS 6s NXDOMAIN is **not** fixed here. |

